<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dorylaeum (1097)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1097</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorylaeum">Dorylaeum</a> was fought on 1 July 1097 near Dorylaeum in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>. The Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-i">Kilij Arslan I</a> attacked the crusader vanguard, but the arrival of the main crusader army turned the battle into a heavy Seljuk defeat. The victory opened Anatolia to the crusaders' march towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and pushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> back to the central plateau.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dorylaeum-1097.jpg" alt="Battle of Dorylaeum (1097)" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown , Guillaume de Tyr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dorylee2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
